# Pinned census of AppKit-notification observers in the shipped Swift target.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# macOS 27 fires AppKit notifications from INSIDE window operations. On
# 2026-08-07 a sample caught the main thread pinned 93/93 inside
# `_NSPopoverCloseAndAnimate → becomeKeyWindow → refreshThreadsFromExternalChange`
# — a popover close storming an `object: nil` observer that re-read disk on
# every callout. Fixed in d79781b1 by coalescing onto the next main-queue tick.
#
# The fix is one site. The RULE is the class: every new AppKit-notification
# observer has to answer "what happens when AppKit fires this a hundred times
# inside one window operation?" This file makes that question unavoidable —
# `scripts/smoke-macos27.sh` fails when the live census stops matching the pin,
# so a new observer cannot land without a reviewer writing its discipline down.
#
# DISCIPLINE VALUES
# -----------------
#   coalesced      `object: nil` (or broad) observer; the handler MUST defer the
#                  real work to the next main-queue tick, and must do no disk,
#                  no DateFormatter/ICU and no layout inside the callout.
#   object-scoped  observer bound to one specific object; the handler MUST stay
#                  O(1) with no disk and no ICU. Acceptable un-coalesced only
#                  because the sender is a single known object.
#
# FORMAT: <path> | <notification> | <discipline> | <note>
# Comments and blank lines are ignored. Order does not matter.

macos/Codescribe/Screens/AgentChat/AgentChatStore.swift | NSWindow.didBecomeKeyNotification | coalesced | d79781b1 · scheduleExternalThreadsRefresh() defers the disk re-read one tick; every window in the app posts this (object: nil)
macos/Codescribe/Screens/AgentChat/MessageList.swift | NSScrollView.willStartLiveScrollNotification | object-scoped | bound to the chat scroll view; handler only emits .userScrollBegan
macos/Codescribe/Screens/AgentChat/MessageList.swift | NSScrollView.didLiveScrollNotification | object-scoped | fires per scroll tick; handler is documentVisibleRect math only — keep it allocation-free
macos/Codescribe/Screens/AgentChat/MessageList.swift | NSScrollView.didEndLiveScrollNotification | object-scoped | bound to the chat scroll view; handler is the same O(1) viewport report
